    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2eff3201_da60e248",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1071489
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-28T11:54:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that the ABR code is written on top of\nthe existing LDAC code in libldacBT_enc.\n\nEven though logically the ABR component is separate from the\nbase LDAC encoder, Is there a reason to create it as a separate shared library instead of all code being within a single library?\n\nThe ABR functionality is useful enough and its size is very small, so\nthere is very little gain (if any) to keep it in a separate library.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3caae221a12d556486a4a7906228ca9ec0d915c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de5a1ea9_60961189",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120881
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-01T02:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can understand your opinion, but I believe it is better  to separate shared library of the ABR and the LDAC.\nBecause, they have different API function to get handle and to initialize. I think those function should be only one in a single shared library.\nAlso, as we reported at the last meeting, it would be better to tune the ABR function on the actual device. To make this process easier, I think the ABR functions should be in a single shared library.",
      "parentUuid": "2eff3201_da60e248",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3caae221a12d556486a4a7906228ca9ec0d915c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
